<title>POLAND: Polish net forex reserves up to $22.17 bln in June.</title>
<headline>Polish net forex reserves up to $22.17 bln in June.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's net foreign currency reserves grew by $459 million in June 1-20 to $22.172 billion and were $630 million higher than in June 1996, the National Bank of Poland said on Thursday.  </p>
<p> POLISH RESERVES (bln dollars)   JUNE 20	MAY     JUNE 1996</p>
<p> Net reserves		     22.172	21.713     21.542</p>
<p> Official reserves		 N/A	   N/A	 17.640</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures in billions of dollars. Official reserves are those held by the state. Net reserves mean the total amount of hard currencies in the whole banking system.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
